Input: {"question": "When was the Poplar station opened?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d00", "start": 0, "end": 142, "text": "Poplar (East India Road) railway station Poplar (East India Road) was a railway station located on the East India Dock Road in Poplar, London."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d00", "start": 143, "end": 193, "text": "It was opened in 1866 by the North London Railway."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d00", "start": 194, "end": 420, "text": "It was the southern passenger terminus of the NLR, although goods trains ran on to connect to the London and Blackwall Railway (LBR) for the East India Docks or to the LBR's Millwall Extension Railway for the West India Docks."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d00", "start": 421, "end": 559, "text": "The station was named Poplar but the LBR also had a station of the same name nearby on Brunswick Street, close to the northern entrance of"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d01", "start": 0, "end": 378, "text": "Disused Stations : Poplar East India Road Station Station Name : POPLAR EAST INDIA ROAD [ Source : Nick Catford ] Date opened : 1.8.1866 Location : South side of East India Dock Road Company on opening : North London Railway Date closed to passengers : 15.5.1944 Date closed completely : 23.4.1945 Company on closing : London & North Western Railway Present state : Demolished ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d01", "start": 379, "end": 457, "text": "The site is now occupied by the Dockhand Light Railway 's All Saints Station ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d01", "start": 458, "end": 568, "text": "The Station Cars office adjacent to All Saints Station entrance occupies the only remaining part of a range of"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d02", "start": 0, "end": 242, "text": "Poplar railway station Poplar was a railway station in Poplar, London, that was opened in 1840 by the Commercial Railway (later the London and Blackwall Railway (LBR)) and was situated between Millwall Junction and Blackwall, down-line from ."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d02", "start": 243, "end": 333, "text": "It was closed in 1926, at which time it was owned by the London and North Eastern Railway."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d02", "start": 334, "end": 522, "text": "The station was opened on 6 July 1840 on the west side of Brunswick Street, to the north of the Blackwall Yard shipyard, but was re-sited five years later across the road to the east side."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d02", "start": 523, "end": 562, "text": "It remained open until 4 May 1926, when"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d03", "start": 0, "end": 41, "text": ", see Poplar station ( disambiguation ) ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d03", "start": 42, "end": 557, "text": "Poplar Poplar railway station in 1962 Location Poplar Grid reference TQ384806 Owner London and Blackwall Railway Key dates 6 July 1840 ( 1840-07-06 ) Opened 1845 [ 1 ] Re-sited 4 May 1926 ( 1926-05-04 ) Closed Other information London transport portal Poplar was a railway station in Poplar , London , that was opened in 1840 by the Commercial Railway ( later the London and Blackwall Railway ( LBR ) ) and was situated between Millwall Junction and Blackwall , 3 miles 16 chains ( 5.1 km ) down-line from Fenchurch"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d04", "start": 0, "end": 96, "text": "Poplar DLR station Poplar is a Docklands Light Railway (DLR) station in Poplar, London, England."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d04", "start": 97, "end": 306, "text": "The station is close to Canary Wharf and is an interchange station for three of the six lines on the DLR (-, Bank- and Tower Gateway-) making it one of the busiest stations on the network in terms of services."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d04", "start": 307, "end": 402, "text": "Long before the opening of the DLR in 1987, there had been three stations with the name Poplar."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d04", "start": 403, "end": 456, "text": "However, none was on the site of the current station."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d04", "start": 457, "end": 559, "text": "Poplar DLR station was opened on 21 August 1987, originally with just two platforms, being served only"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d05", "start": 0, "end": 116, "text": "sited due south of the North London Railway station ( now All Saints DLR ) , and due east of the present DLR depot ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d05", "start": 117, "end": 273, "text": "Poplar DLR station was opened on 21 August 1987 , originally with just two platforms , being served only by the Stratford-Island Gardens branch of the DLR ."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d05", "start": 274, "end": 417, "text": "As the DLR was expanded eastwards , the station was extensively remodelled , given two extra platforms and expanded to take two-car operation ."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d05", "start": 418, "end": 531, "text": "On 28 March 1994 Poplar became the western terminus of the new Beckton branch , which opened the same day ; on 31"}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "1866", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0371-73a80c4c2111:d00:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C1", 